From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:47:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: log the ARM64EC map without reading a PEB that does
 not exist yet

alloc_arm64ec_map logged peb->EcCodeBitMap after setting it only when
there is a PEB. Since wine-11.18 the PEB is made after the main image is
mapped (virtual_alloc_first_teb, from init_startup_info), so an ARM64EC
main image reaches alloc_arm64ec_map with peb NULL, and the log line read
0x368: the app aborted in update_arm64ec_ranges <- virtual_map_image <-
virtual_map_main_module <- load_main_exe <- __wine_main. An x86-64 main
image maps its ARM64EC DLLs after the PEB exists, which is why no title
hit it. The line now logs the map itself; virtual_alloc_first_teb already
gives the PEB the map when it makes it.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-child-process.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index f5b398e..2f0e693 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -13501,8 +13501,14 @@ static void alloc_arm64ec_map(void)
     if (peb) peb->EcCodeBitMap = arm64ec_view->base;
     /* ml127: dprintf, not ERR — the `virtual` channel's ERR is suppressed in
      * this build, which is why this line has never once appeared in a log. */
-    dprintf(2, "[ec-map] peb->EcCodeBitMap=%p size=0x%lx (%lu MB)\n",
-            peb->EcCodeBitMap, (unsigned long)size, (unsigned long)(size >> 20));
+    /* Playport: log the map, not peb->EcCodeBitMap. Since wine-11.18 the PEB
+     * is made after the main image is mapped (virtual_alloc_first_teb), so an
+     * ARM64EC main image gets here with peb NULL, and reading its
+     * EcCodeBitMap (at 0x368) aborted the app in update_arm64ec_ranges.
+     * virtual_alloc_first_teb gives the PEB the map when it makes it. */
+    dprintf(2, "[ec-map] EcCodeBitMap=%p size=0x%lx (%lu MB)%s\n",
+            arm64ec_view->base, (unsigned long)size, (unsigned long)(size >> 20),
+            peb ? "" : " (no PEB yet: the first TEB gets it)");
 }
 
 
